        "page": 11,
        "quote": "Rosenberg received a Beit Fellowship for Scientific Researchof the annual value of £2407 from the Imperial College of Science, Technology, and Medicine, South Kensington, in London to undertake theoretical investigations in topics connected with quantum mechanics and obtain a Diploma of Membership of the Imperial College of Science and Technology(D.I.C.), an academic certiﬁcate awarded to postgraduate students upon graduation. He stayed there from October 1932 to July 1934 in the Department of Mathematics."
      }
